# Bot1 attacks with Jacked Rabbit and Adeline, whose attack triggers go on the stack together, and takes the order the
# client's Stack Triggers box lays out rather than picking one (CR 603.3b). The box shows them in the order they
# triggered — the Rabbit's first, Adeline's second — and its Stack All button sends exactly that, which is what
# clicking them left to right would have sent.
#
# The first one shown goes on the stack first, so it ends up at the bottom and resolves last: the stack reads Adeline
# over Jacked Rabbit. That is the direction the box promises with "the last one on resolves first".

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Adeline, Resplendent Cathar
Plains
Jacked Rabbit
Plains
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Adeline, Resplendent Cathar.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Jacked Rabbit.Cast(X: 2)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Adeline, Resplendent Cathar; Jacked Rabbit)
Bot1.Triggers(Jacked Rabbit; Adeline, Resplendent Cathar)
? Stack.Count = 2
? Stack = Adeline, Resplendent Cathar; Jacked Rabbit

[Expect]
Turn = 5
